I'm not sure you need a pre-written rhetorical script, but here are some general suggestions that might help you improve your approach:

- Re-read the resolution and bring it out of your head and onto a piece of paper;
- Identify what you don't care to argue about, and focus on the part of the resolution that you do;
- Think about whether AI usage is a "lawmaker" or an "umpire" role in society, and what kind of implications this will have for your arguments. Note that law enforcement and government uses are different from other uses.
